----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Case 5: vacuum_defer_cleanup_age holds the recycle back on the primary,
-- and with it the conflict, as it holds back heap cleanup.  For a standby
-- that cannot feed its xmin back to the source (no hot_standby_feedback)
-- it is the knob that delays this conflict.  The reader may be cancelled
-- by any of the deferred cleanups the second VACUUM releases, so this
-- case does not use the relfilenode probe; it only shows that the
-- deferred VACUUM spares the reader and the later one does not.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
!\retcode gpconfig -c vacuum_defer_cleanup_age -v 1;
